        "math_academy_id": "q-183689",
        "problem": "Describe the set $S={1,2,3,\u2026,29}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nN\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers less than or equal to $29.$\n\nIn other words, $S$ contains all natural numbers less than $30,$ *excluding* $30.$\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as \n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x<30}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,0<x<30}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $x\\le 29.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x\\le 29},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:1\\le x\\le 29}.\n$$",
